{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":71514588,"ns":0,"title":"Approximate fibration","extract":"In algebraic topology, a branch of mathematics, an approximate fibration is a sort of fibration such that the homotopy lifting property holds only approximately. The notion was introduced by Coram and Duvall in 1977.","description":"Mathematical concept","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}